Z||000008||Wade87GT||07-20-2000||03:36 PM||||Hey coyote, yours is the exact setup I've been pondering for months. Thanks for providing a photo of my mental image. How difficult was it to knock out the bumpstop mounts? Also, you comfortable are you with the idea of using your springs and shocks as bumpstops? My car is still a daily driver, bad roads and all.<BR>Thanks,<BR>Wade||||reg||5
Z||000009||coyote||07-20-2000||03:50 PM||||Wade87GT:<BR>It is not to difficult to remove the bump stop, It is spotwelded in three places. I used a sharp chisle and a hammer and went to town, it took a couple of hours. the springs and shocks are built to take the beating. It is essentially the same set-up just in coil over form. even in stock form you would have to really be driving over some tuff terrain to bottom the suspension out.<P>Coyote<BR>84 SE<BR>87 GT||||reg||1
Z||000010||bHooper||07-20-2000||04:45 PM||||niiiiccccce!<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT||||reg||1
Z||000011||Archie||07-21-2000||12:09 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by coyote:<BR><B>Stock brakes??? No way.  Actually cadillac in fron Camaro in the rear. All part we ureathane bushed as well.  Car is not complete. When the engine conversion is complete i will let you know how it goes.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Come on, Come on Scott...... Tell the whole story. Those pictures are pictures of Jack Wagners car when it was at my shop for a LT1 swap...... they were taken several months ago when you USED to work for me. Jack is already driving the car, he's had it for quite a while. If you plan on reporting on it's performance, you'll have to convince Jack that he should let you drive it. I see no reason why he will do that. BTW, I did drive it extensively. Just so the facts are straight.... the car has RCC coil overs and "A" arms. The front spindles were from Ryanne. The calipers were Camaro Front & Caddy rear and were mounted using the brake mounting system I have "on the shelf".<P>Archie||||reg||4
Z||000012||Dan86gt3.8||07-21-2000||01:20 AM||||archie up late?<P>------------------<BR>86 gt fiero<BR>3.8/4speed auto<BR>ace conversion kit<BR>15" konig monsoon's<BR>rear swaybar/ and urethane on rear.<BR>Soon to come urethane all the way around. and new yellow paint w/ raised spoiler!!!!<BR>(also in way future years forced induction on my 3.8!!!!!!!!!)||||reg||1
