Z||000016||fierov8||07-21-2000||01:45 PM||||Archie/Coyote,<P>Interesting -- went to Ryane's site and all that they list for a pre-88 is a 1.5" drop spindle.  They also state that you have to use their 12" brake upgrade kit.<P>Sooo -- my questions:<P>* Is that a custom spindle on the pictured car?<P>* I have a soon-to-be-delivered Corvette big brake kit from RCC that I want to use on my '86.  Since you guys know both vendors better than I do -- is it possible to use the RCC brake kit with the Ryane drop sppindle?<P>thx,<P>-jeff dutkofski<BR>Fort Worth, TX||||reg||1
Z||000017||Archie||07-21-2000||02:21 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fierov8:<BR><B>Archie/Coyote,<P>Sooo -- my questions:<P>* Is that a custom spindle on the pictured car?<P>* is it possible to use the RCC brake kit with the Ryane drop sppindle?<P>thx,<P>-jeff dutkofski<BR>Fort Worth, TX</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The Spindle is a Ryanne and yes to the RCC thing.<P>Archie||||reg||1
